#!/bin/bash
# jobrun NAME MAXAGE command...
# Runs a scheduled job and records when it last succeeded, for jobwatch.py (-> Kuma "Scheduled jobs").
# MAXAGE = seconds without a success before the watchdog calls the job late. Exit code is passed through.
name=$1 maxage=$2; shift 2
"$@"; rc=$?
d="$HOME/.jobs"; mkdir -p "$d"
if [ "$rc" -eq 0 ]; then echo "$(date +%s) $maxage" > "$d/$name.ok"; else echo "$(date +%s) $rc" > "$d/$name.fail"; fi
exit "$rc"
